## Why This Is Asked
Tests few-shot, on-device adaptation, and robust pose estimation under occlusion and motion.

## Key Concepts
- Few-shot on-device adaptation; - monocular 6-DoF pose; - temporal consistency; - synthetic-to-real data.

## Code Example
```javascript
function weightedLoss(posePred, poseGT, maskPred, maskGT){
  const Lp = l2(posePred, poseGT);
  const Lm = crossEntropy(maskPred, maskGT);
  return Lp + Lm;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend to more than 3-shot adaptation with minimal latency?
- How would you evaluate failure modes under strong motion blur and fabric reflectivity?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a complete edge-CV pipeline: real-time monocular 3D pose with per-object velocity, occlusion robustness, and rapid on-device adaptation to unseen parts. Emphasizes practical data strategies and evaluation in an industrial setting.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time monocular 3D pose estimation
- Per-instance velocity prediction for planning
- On-device few-shot adaptation (5-shot)
- Occlusion handling and data fusion strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: forward pass with adaptation trigger
function forward(frame, exemplars){
  let features = backbone(frame);
  let detections = detector(features);
  let poses = poseHead(features, detections);
  let vel = velocityHead(features, detections, previous);
  if (exemplars) adapt(poses, exemplars);
  return {detections, poses, vel};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify robustness to occlusion in your evaluation?
- What ablation would you run to isolate the velocity head contribution?

## Why This Is Asked
Realistic disaster-response CV requires monocular depth, 3D reconstruction, and hazard awareness on constrained hardware.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular depth priors, 3D reconstruction, multi-task heads, temporal fusion, few-shot on-device adaptation.
- Edge GPU latency budgeting and data synthesis.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-training loop
for (const frame of video) {
  const pred = model(frame);
  const loss = computeLoss(pred, target);
  optimizer.step(loss);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would domain gap between synthetic and real data affect adaptation?
- What ablations would you run to diagnose latency vs accuracy trade-offs?
